WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.220
Good morning, John. It's Wednesday.

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:02.480
Argh!

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:04.320
[John]: Ah, chair wars!

00:00:04.555 --> 00:00:07.695
You say it's Wednesday? It's question Wednesday, the day that I answer real questions from real nerdfighters.

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:10.219
Number one: "What was your biggest childhood argument?"

00:00:10.219 --> 00:00:11.899
[Hank]: I think that you lying is the problem

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:15.140
where y- where something would happen, you would lie, and I would get blamed,

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:16.960
because you were a better liar than I was.

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:18.720
You're still a much better liar than I am.

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:19.800
[John]: I'm a novelist.

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:20.540
[Hank laughs]

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:21.540
[John]: It's, like, my job.

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:23.840
How come you guys never come to Ireland or even mention it?

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:26.180
[Hank]: Um, mentioned. [John]: Done.

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:28.300
Would you rather have a unicorn or a Pegasus?

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:30.120
[Hank]: A Pegasus, obviously. [John]: Really?

00:00:30.122 --> 00:00:31.108
[John]: No. [Hank]: Yes.

00:00:31.108 --> 00:00:31.708
[Hank]: It has wings.

00:00:31.708 --> 00:00:33.560
[John]: But if you had a unicorn, you could kill it.

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:35.660
[Hank]: Well, you could kill the Pegasus too, if you wanted to.

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:37.960
You can ride a unicorn, it's like - it's just a frickin' horse.

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:39.760
It's like: Would you rather have a horse or a flying horse?

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:44.660
[John]: "Is it possible that The Giant Squid of Anger and the Sarlac from Star Wars share an evolutionary link?"

00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:47.660
[Hank]: No. It's not, because that happened in a galaxy far, far away

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:50.800
and there's no way to transmit genetic material between galaxies.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:52.120
[John]: It's also a long time ago.

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:54.780
[Hank]: Right. That's not.. that's not as big of a problem.

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:56.060
[John]: It's more the far, far away. [Hank]: Yeah.

00:00:56.060 --> 00:00:57.740
[John]: "Why does the internet love bacon so much?"

00:00:57.740 --> 00:00:59.020
[Hank]: Because bacon is delicious.

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:01.160
[John]: (With Southern accent) Yeah, bacon is good fer me.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:05.640
Do you ever see those, uh, those anti-piracy ads, that are like: "You wouldn't download bacon."

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:07.540
And I'm like: "Yes I would."

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:10.760
[Hank]: If it was possible. [John]: Is that- is that a thing? We can download bacon?!

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:11.640
[Makes downloading noise]

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:14.060
[John Laughs] Does it come out of my printer?

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:16.680
"What's your favourite thing about each other?"

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:18.060
[Hank]: I like... this part.

00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:24.080
[John]: Hahaha that's totally creepy. You just inspired a very unfortunate generation of fan fiction writers.

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:26.680
[Hank]: I think there's gonna be a Facebook fan page for this part.

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:28.140
What's up?

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:31.120
[John]: I was giving them some of that part. [Hank]: Oh [John]: So that they could make the screen cap.

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:33.720
[Hank]: I thought you found something up on my ceiling that I should know about. [John]: Ooh, look at that.

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:34.940
Wow, you have Kermit up there.

00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:36.840
[Hank]: He's just, you know, my household god.

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:41.740
[John]: I mean, I have, that's where I have Padre Pio. I have a Roman Catholic saint and you have Kermit.

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:46.260
[Hank]: I figured Padre Pio was a soccer player. [Both laugh] Just assumed!

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:48.740
[John]: "Have you seen the new modernised version of Sherlock Holmes?"

00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:52.260
[Hank]: Are we talking about the Cumberbatch one or the- the Downey Jr. one?

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:53.840
[John]: Because the Cumberbatch.. [Hank]: I've seen both.

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:56.720
[John]: The Cumberbatch one: 2 thumbs up. [Hank]: Yeees.

00:01:57.020 --> 00:02:00.980
[John]: The Downey Jr. one: one thumb... like... [Hank]: Yeah

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:02.820
See, we don't disagree! [Both]: We don't disagree!

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:04.202
[John]: "Arm wrestling maatch!"

00:02:04.202 --> 00:02:05.392
[Hank]: Aaarm wrestling match!

00:02:05.392 --> 00:02:07.472
[John]: One, two, three.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:14.600
[Their voices are sped up]

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:17.560
[John]: I give up, I give up! Argh... Aw...

00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:19.600
"Do you guys go back and watch your old videos?"

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:22.074
[Hank]: That implies that we've ever watched an old video.

00:02:22.074 --> 00:02:25.374
I never watch... [John]: Haha You never watch Brotherhood 2.0?

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:26.340
[Hank]: I've never seen the show.

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:28.540
[John]: I really enjoy watching the old videos, particularly your old videos.

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:30.180
When I watch my old videos, I'm pretty hard on myself.

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:34.460
[Hank]: It's funny because I like to watch my old videos too. [John laughs] I'm like that guy is so funny oh my god!

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:37.580
[John]: "Why do you do the things you do? Wouldn't it be easier to just play games all day?

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:39.600
What is the point of doing things in general?"

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:43.880
[John]: Wow. That's a...  [Hank]: What is the point of doing things in general?

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:47.240
There is no reason to do things. There's no, like, cosmic mandate to do stuff.

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:49.614
[John]: I feel bad for that person.

00:02:49.614 --> 00:02:54.334
Because I've struggled with that a lot. In fact, I wrote a novel about it called "The Fault in Our Stars."

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:56.779
[Hank]: It's available in a link below. All copies will be signed.

00:02:56.779 --> 00:03:00.419
[John]: Since there isn't, as you said, a cosmic mandate to do things, you know?

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:06.120
There isn't a cosmic mandate to make stuff, and the world probably won't be any different as

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:07.920
a result of the stuff that you make or do.

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:08.940
[Hank]: I think it's human nature.

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:11.580
I think that we have a human nature to like to do stuff and interact with people

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:14.920
and to make the world better for each other. [John]: Yeah. [Hank]: I think that we like doing that.

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:17.780
[John]: Yeah, making stuff is very fulfilling in and of itself

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:20.020
in a way that playing video games isn't. [Hank]: Even if it's making a garden bed

00:03:20.020 --> 00:03:23.220
or if it's making... I mean, even you know video games are set up to do that.

00:03:23.229 --> 00:03:24.989
They're set up to satisfy that need.

00:03:24.989 --> 00:03:28.129
[John]: Right. Uh, but they can also become kind of insular.

00:03:28.129 --> 00:03:30.849
[Hank]: Right, no, I mean they're set up to satisfy that need in a very shallow way.

00:03:30.849 --> 00:03:32.829
[John]: We love making awesome stuff with awesome people.

00:03:32.829 --> 00:03:37.960
That's what we've always loved and we feel very lucky to be part of a community where that stuff happens.

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:40.120
[Hank]: I'm going to turn that, right there, into a song.

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:42.120
[John]: Are you? [Hank]: I'm going to Songify it.

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:44.220
[John]: Is it going to be called "Making Awesome Stuff with Awesome People?"

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:45.520
Oh, you're gonna Songify me?

00:03:45.526 --> 00:03:47.181
I'm gonna sing on key for once?!

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:50.180
[Hank]: I can't actually, I do not have that technology. [John laughs]

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:53.240
John, thank you for doing my first Question Tuesday ever with me.

00:03:53.240 --> 00:03:55.400
[John]: It's been a privilege. [Hank]: And I will see you right now.

00:03:55.940 --> 00:03:57.700
[John]: I will continue to see you.

00:03:57.880 --> 00:03:58.740
[Hank]: Stop looking at me.

00:03:59.096 --> 00:04:00.120
Stop looking at me!

